WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.459 --> 00:00:04.295
I was just thinking about how,
like, in LA,

00:00:04.379 --> 00:00:07.298
how quickly people
will get on the bandwagon,

00:00:07.382 --> 00:00:12.679
like, I tell people,
"Oh, there's an event, be here."

00:00:12.762 --> 00:00:14.472
How quickly they go to do that.

00:00:14.556 --> 00:00:18.059
And I don't...
understand why, like...

00:00:21.187 --> 00:00:25.942
people have a harder time doing that
in terms of when it comes to the earth.

00:00:44.377 --> 00:00:45.587
They're going to go.

00:00:50.300 --> 00:00:53.178
Hi, I'm Lana Condor
and I'm in the Maasai Mara

00:00:53.261 --> 00:00:54.429
with Netflix's Our Planet.

00:00:56.806 --> 00:00:58.266
-Hello.
-Hi.

00:00:59.225 --> 00:01:00.518
It's a mad, mad world here.

00:01:00.602 --> 00:01:03.271
We landed.
There's some zebra right over here.

00:01:03.772 --> 00:01:05.357
-There's some...
-No!

00:01:05.648 --> 00:01:06.900
Whatever the hell those are.

00:01:06.983 --> 00:01:11.863
The Mara is one of the places in Africa
that has the most wildlife.

00:01:11.946 --> 00:01:13.448
They're standing up on there,
back a little.

00:01:13.531 --> 00:01:15.283
Oh, my gosh. No way.

00:01:16.034 --> 00:01:16.868
Is that a hippo?

00:01:16.951 --> 00:01:18.328
There's little bubbles coming up.

00:01:18.411 --> 00:01:19.871
Right there.
Like, way down there.

00:01:19.954 --> 00:01:21.456
Like, right the way down, yeah.

00:01:22.832 --> 00:01:23.708
Oh, my God.

00:01:23.792 --> 00:01:26.920
Wait, how long
have we been here, 15 minutes?

00:01:27.003 --> 00:01:29.756
So, it was, like... I was, like,
literally touched down in the Mara

00:01:29.839 --> 00:01:32.842
for, like, the first ten minutes,
and I'm already watching

00:01:32.926 --> 00:01:37.430
these lions feed on this buffalo.

00:01:39.474 --> 00:01:41.810
Plus, they're not just lions
that are there...

00:01:41.893 --> 00:01:43.395
It's hyenas...

00:01:43.812 --> 00:01:45.397
And there are jackals there.

00:01:45.480 --> 00:01:49.693
I was blown away because the buffalo
provided for all of them.

00:01:51.111 --> 00:01:52.570
Amazing.

00:01:52.987 --> 00:01:54.322
OK.

00:01:54.406 --> 00:01:59.452
We just got put in our tents,

00:01:59.536 --> 00:02:02.080
right out here is the river.

00:02:02.163 --> 00:02:05.333
There are four hippos right here.

00:02:05.417 --> 00:02:08.169
It is unbelievable.

00:02:13.466 --> 00:02:17.846
Well, being out here really, like,
changes the way that you see things.

00:02:18.513 --> 00:02:20.473
Hello, baby.

00:02:21.433 --> 00:02:22.475
Oh, my God.

00:02:22.559 --> 00:02:25.603
Holy... shit.
Holy shit. Holy shit.

00:02:27.647 --> 00:02:28.481
You're OK.

00:02:29.399 --> 00:02:31.568
Oh, my God. He's up.
He's up, he's up!

00:02:31.651 --> 00:02:33.028
-He's up.
-He's up!

00:02:33.570 --> 00:02:35.155
-He's up!
-Yes!

00:02:35.655 --> 00:02:36.990
Oh, down.

00:02:37.073 --> 00:02:40.035
So, I'm seeing the mom eat her placenta

00:02:40.118 --> 00:02:43.997
and the baby find her milk
for the first time.

00:02:46.541 --> 00:02:48.084
You got it. Good job.

00:02:50.128 --> 00:02:51.546
Get out of the way.

00:02:51.671 --> 00:02:53.631
This baby's, like, "I'm stressed."

00:02:57.719 --> 00:02:59.012
Where's the...

00:03:00.388 --> 00:03:01.765
Are we going to see the leopard?

00:03:02.223 --> 00:03:03.266
We're going to see a leopard?

00:03:07.187 --> 00:03:08.938
Oh, wow.

00:03:14.152 --> 00:03:15.695
He's looking straight at us.

00:03:20.533 --> 00:03:21.660
Yeah.

00:03:22.369 --> 00:03:25.497
I feel like this is one of
the first animals that we've seen

00:03:26.122 --> 00:03:28.833
that notice us.

00:03:28.917 --> 00:03:30.835
Or at least acknowledge us.

00:03:31.461 --> 00:03:33.588
But I was thinking...
I was thinking, like,

00:03:33.672 --> 00:03:39.511
how quickly... everyone, like,
got in their cars and drove...

00:03:42.222 --> 00:03:44.057
so quickly to see...

00:03:47.060 --> 00:03:50.355
How quickly people got in
their cars to see the leopard,

00:03:50.438 --> 00:03:52.565
and then I was just thinking
about how, like...

00:03:53.441 --> 00:03:55.318
the earth just seems so big.

00:04:00.699 --> 00:04:02.826
So, maybe that's why we think
that it's really hard,

00:04:02.909 --> 00:04:03.994
'cause it's like...

00:04:04.536 --> 00:04:07.497
It's so big that we can't even
wrap our head around the problem.

00:04:08.999 --> 00:04:10.125
And I can grasp...

00:04:10.208 --> 00:04:12.669
I can understand that
a little bit better.

00:04:13.211 --> 00:04:17.048
Animals and the people
who live here need space.

00:04:17.132 --> 00:04:20.051
And when people keep
taking it away or things change...

00:04:22.262 --> 00:04:24.264
it makes me sad because I feel like...

00:04:24.723 --> 00:04:27.267
there's... there's room for everyone.

00:04:32.105 --> 00:04:33.273
Oh, look at her!

00:04:33.356 --> 00:04:36.901
Oh, my gosh.
Oh, my gosh. Wow.

00:04:49.039 --> 00:04:50.415
That was the trip.

00:04:50.498 --> 00:04:52.042
That was so amazing.

00:04:53.335 --> 00:04:57.088
Now that I've been here
for three and a half days,

00:04:57.172 --> 00:05:00.508
I can honestly say that it truly is
a life changing experience.

00:05:02.385 --> 00:05:05.472
We saw a lot of babies,
and then we saw a lot of big things.

00:05:07.265 --> 00:05:09.351
But it terms of our planet,

00:05:09.434 --> 00:05:13.355
you really kind of understand
that whole circle of life.

00:05:13.438 --> 00:05:16.066
And you learn we're out here to coexist.

00:05:16.149 --> 00:05:17.567
We're not out here to dominate.

00:05:17.651 --> 00:05:19.778
Or else this beauty will go away.

00:05:20.820 --> 00:05:23.698
This is the closest I've ever felt,

00:05:23.782 --> 00:05:25.700
to have my feet on the ground
and be grounded

00:05:25.784 --> 00:05:28.453
and as a part of our planet earth.

00:05:28.703 --> 00:05:29.829
Look at this!

00:05:30.330 --> 00:05:32.707
It's a full rainbow!

00:05:33.166 --> 00:05:36.503
This is everyone's home,
and we must protect it.

